From fb893d061a6caf1ee73b7d53a53c020b09943254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:25:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] microblaze: Implement the ucontext functions

MicroBlaze has only ever had the generic ENOSYS stubs of getcontext,
setcontext, swapcontext and makecontext, so the stdlib/tst-setcontext*
and tst-swapcontext* tests fail and anything using ucontext (coroutine
libraries, some interpreters) does not work on this target.

getcontext saves r1, r2, r13, r15 and the callee-saved r19-r31 into
uc_mcontext.regs, records the resume address r15 + 8 in the pc slot,
and reads the signal mask with rt_sigprocmask.  setcontext restores
the mask, the argument registers r5-r10 (for a context set up by
makecontext), the saved registers, and jumps to pc with r3 = 0.
swapcontext does both with a single rt_sigprocmask call.  setcontext
and swapcontext keep ucp in r19 across the system call, and keep the
caller's r19 in the r5 save slot that the caller reserves, so that a
failing call returns -1 with r19 intact.

makecontext lays out the stack with the 28-byte area the ABI reserves
at the callee's sp (link slot plus six argument save slots) and any
arguments beyond the sixth above it, keeps uc_link in the callee-saved
r19, and sets r15 to __startcontext - 8 so the function's "rtsd r15,8"
returns to __startcontext, which resumes uc_link or calls exit.
__startcontext is preceded by padding so that an unwinder's lookup of
the address before it does not find __setcontext, as on sparc
(BZ #22919, BZ #34978).

The symbols already exist in the ABI list as the stubs, so no new
version is needed.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
